<h2>Licensing Terms</h2>
Here are the license terms:
<ol>
  <li> Data Files - The bulk of the data in the ISFDB has been entered by the public,
  either via the online forms or through private databases which have been merged
  into the ISFDB. On the other hand, some data (such as that from NESFA) was obtained
  with the proviso that the data not be used for commercial purposes. As such, the
  data files in the ISFDB may be freely used to create derived works, so long as they
  are non-commercial in nature. Attributions to the ISFDB should be made.
  Commercial use of the files cannot be permitted.
  <p>
  <li> Awards Data Files - We have purposely disallowed the entry of awards information
  at the ISFDB. This means that all of the data can be tracked to threthree specific people.
  As such, copyright of the awards files is held by Al von Ruff, Paul Cardinal, and
  David G. Grubbs. Each award file contains a copyright citation to this effect.
  We have decided that you may use the data contained within the awards files to
  create derived works, so long as they are non-commercial in nature, and an
  attribution to the ISFDB is made. Commercial use of the files must be negotiated
  with the parties cited in the copyright notice.
  <p>
  <li> Source Code - at present, all ISFDB source code copyrights are held by Al von Ruff. 
  You may use the source code to create derived works, so long as they are non-commercial
  in nature, and an attribution to the ISFDB is made.
</ol>

